  "name": "Savoy opera (Gilbert and Sullivan comic opera)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "The comic operas written by W. S. Gilbert and Arthur Sullivan between 1871 and 1896 and most of them produced by Richard D'Oyly Carte and named after the Savoy Theatre in London that Carte built for them in 1881, among them H.M.S. Pinafore, The Pirates of Penzance, The Mikado and The Gondoliers. The D'Oyly Carte Opera Company kept the performing tradition as a fixed house style and recorded the canon repeatedly, for HMV and from 1949 for Decca, until the company closed in 1982.",
